messages:
maria: Hey team — noticed onboarding README's Node example uses top-level await and ESM import but the snippet label says "CommonJS". Users copy/pasting into older projects hit a runtime SyntaxError. Repro steps: create new project with 'type': 'commonjs' and paste snippet.
kevin: Oof. Can you paste the exact broken snippet? I can open a quick PR.
maria: Broken (from README):
```
import Redwood from 'redwood-inference';
const client = new Redwood();
const resp = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood/4x', prompt: 'hi' });
console.log(resp.text);
```
This will throw in CommonJS or Node <14 without --experimental-modules. Also the auth header example shows `REDACTED_TOKEN` which confuses folks who then paste the placeholder into code.
docs-bot: FYI: There were 3 support tickets in the last 48h referencing the same copy/paste issue (refs: #5432, #5438, #5441).
ben: Suggestion: provide two variants and a minimal snippet that uses promises instead of top-level await. e.g.
```
const Redwood = require('redwood-inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
client.generate({ model: 'redwood/4x', prompt: 'hi' })
  .then(resp => console.log(resp.text))
  .catch(err => console.error(err));
```
Also add a note under the snippet: "If you're using ESM/Node >=14 with 'type':'module', use top-level await; otherwise use promises or an async IIFE." :memo:
sam: I'll take the PR. Maria — can you add the failing repro and the suggested replacements in the PR description? Also update the placeholder token text to 'process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY' to reduce copy/paste mistakes.
maria: Yep. Opening PR now: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/678 — includes tests in the sample-app that run the snippet via node:12/14/18 matrix. @kevin can you review the concurrency section too? thanks!
kevin: Reviewing now. Quick note — let's also separate the minimal auth example from the full sdk example so it's obvious which env var to set. :thumbsup:
